            <h2>Route Overview: Chicago to Ann Arbor</h2>
            <p>Traveling from Chicago to Ann Arbor by train is one of the most convenient and scenic ways to connect the Midwest's largest city with one of Michigan's most vibrant college towns. This route is primarily served by Amtrak's Wolverine service, offering direct connections that make it a preferred choice for students, business travelers, and leisure visitors alike. The journey spans across Illinois, Indiana, and Michigan, providing travelers with a comfortable and reliable alternative to driving or flying. </p>
            <p>The Wolverine route is especially popular because it combines practical connectivity with a relaxed travel experience. Unlike air travel, the train delivers passengers directly from downtown Chicago to the heart of Ann Arbor near the University of Michigan campus, eliminating the need for airport transfers and lengthy security procedures. </p>
