            <h2>Understanding the Route Geography</h2>
            <p>The journey from Chicago to Ann Arbor begins at Union Station in downtown Chicago and moves eastward across the Midwest. The route crosses from Illinois into Indiana, skirting the southern shore of Lake Michigan, before entering Michigan and heading northeast toward Ann Arbor. </p>
            <p>The journey passes through diverse landscapes: the urban environment of Chicago gives way to the industrial and lakeshore regions of northern Indiana, followed by the rolling countryside of southwestern Michigan. As the train approaches Ann Arbor, the scenery reflects the character of southeastern Michigan with its mix of suburban development and university-town atmosphere. </p>
