            <h2>Travel Guide: About Chicago</h2>
            <p>Chicago is the third-largest city in the United States and the cultural and economic hub of the Midwest. Known for its architecture, deep-dish pizza, blues music, and lakefront parks, it offers a vibrant urban experience before your onward journey. </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Home to iconic landmarks like Millennium Park, the Willis Tower, and Navy Pier</li>
                <li>A global hub for finance, technology, and the arts</li>
                <li>Well-connected public transport system, making it easy to explore</li>
                <li>World-class museums including the Art Institute of Chicago and Field Museum</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>What This Means for Travelers</h3>
            <p>Chicago is not just a departure point-it is a destination worth exploring. If your schedule allows, spend time walking along the Lakefront Trail, exploring the Magnificent Mile, or enjoying the city's renowned food scene. The city's compact downtown core is easily navigable, and Union Station's central location puts you within reach of major attractions. </p>
            <h3>Things to Do Before Departure</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Explore nearby landmarks: </b> Visit Millennium Park or the Art Institute, both close to Union Station.</li>
                <li><b>Enjoy local cuisine: </b> Try a classic Chicago deep-dish pizza or a Chicago-style hot dog</li>
                <li><b>Take a short walk: </b> Stroll along the Chicago Riverwalk for views of the city's famous architecture</li>
                <li><b>Prepare for your journey: </b> Arrive at Union Station early and check gate information on departure boards.</li>
            </ul>
            <h2>Travel Guide: About Ann Arbor</h2>
            <p>Arriving in Ann Arbor, you step into one of the most dynamic college towns in the United States. Home to the University of Michigan, the city blends academic energy with cultural sophistication, offering world-class museums, vibrant performing arts, and a renowned food scene. </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Home to the University of Michigan, one of America's top public universities</li>
                <li>Known for its progressive culture, arts scene, and intellectual atmosphere</li>
                <li>Historic Kerrytown district with farmers market and boutique shops</li>
                <li>Gateway to Michigan's natural beauty, including the Great Lakes</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>What This Means for Travelers</h3>
            <p>Ann Arbor's station location near downtown means you can begin exploring immediately. The city's compact layout makes it easy to navigate on foot or by bus. Whether you're visiting for university business, exploring the cultural attractions, or using Ann Arbor as a base for Michigan exploration, the train station provides convenient access to everything the city offers. </p>
            <h3>Top Attractions in Ann Arbor</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><b>University of Michigan Campus: </b> Historic central campus with iconic buildings and the Law Quad</li>
                <li><b>Michigan Stadium ("The Big House"):</b> The largest stadium in North America with a capacity over 107,000</li>
                <li><b>University of Michigan Museum of Art (UMMA): </b> Free admission to a world-class art collection</li>
                <li><b>Nichols Arboretum: </b> Beautiful gardens and walking trails along the Huron River</li>
                <li><b>Kerrytown District: </b> Historic neighborhood with the farmers market, shops, and restaurants</li>
