            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3>1. How long is the train from Chicago to Ann Arbor? </h3>
            <p>The train time from Chicago to Ann Arbor typically ranges between 4 hours 14 minutes and 4 hours 45 minutes. The Wolverine service offers direct journeys with consistent travel times. </p>

            <h3>2. What is the fastest train from Chicago to Ann Arbor? </h3>
            <p>The fastest option is the Amtrak Wolverine, which can complete the journey in approximately 4 hours 14 minutes with direct service. </p>

            <h3>3. How much does a train cost from Chicago to Ann Arbor? </h3>
            <p>The train from Chicago to Ann Arbor generally costs between: </p>
            <p>$30 - $50 for early booking (Saver fares) </p>
            <p>$50 - $90 for standard fares (Value tickets) </p>
            <p>$90 - $150+ for last-minute or Flexible fares</p>
            <p>Prices vary based on timing, availability, and class of service. </p>

            <h3>4. Are there direct trains from Chicago to Ann Arbor? </h3>
            <p>Yes, there are direct trains available. The Amtrak Wolverine operates three daily round-trips with direct service between Chicago Union Station and Ann Arbor Station. </p>

